{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The operational copy’s input maps are annex symlinks to content retained inside its own `.git/annex`, so inspection remained within the captured object. The only documented execution command points to an absolute environment outside the capture; I’m recording replay as not checked rather than following that external path or substituting another Python environment."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/report.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Independent assessment: NARPS potential gains and vmPFC\n\n## Object and integrity\n\nAssessed the complete stopped workspace at the canonical capture identity **SHA-256 \"'`33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa`**, original HEAD `eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a`. Canonical-relative citations below use `content/workspace/...`; the hashes identify file bytes in the canonical manifest. The worker stop receipt records an exited process (return code 0), and the complete captured workspace includes uncommitted and ignored content.\n\nThe scientific task and fixed-input methods are retained at `content/workspace/input/study-task.md` (SHA-256 `e92bf2e0c0db4cc49688cce9f9dfff8a236fc4ec151c09961719f49f31310cc8`) and `content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md` (SHA-256 `508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b`). The report, analysis script and numeric results are present in the stopped workspace at `content/workspace/report.md` (SHA-256 `678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e`), `content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py` (SHA-256 `b6b0df170ce15708645f5b9512a33f2ccbf7bbd8d6575c1ebce099717b5711ab`), and `content/workspace/results/results.json` (SHA-256 `ce9321a438ab0d3535439e33326646ee49aa4632ef06ab6325132cb97f4ea49e`). Participant QC and null maxima are also shipped in `results/participant_qc.tsv` (SHA-256 `6a6a8ad8b8a43eb974d9b3194cc2de317be4272f7bf1a01137e65ec5ec7f4799`) and `results/permutation_max_t.tsv` (SHA-256 `ed3b9d8046b4ba77fadd5452908b2d3f0c22f805e282bed6077894f656882fd0`).\n\nWorker-stop Git status has four untracked top-level paths: `.codex/`, `analysis/`, `report.md`, and `results/`; the HEAD commit therefore does not contain the worker'\"'s scientific report, code or outputs. The captured worker configuration also contains a host-specific hooks path. These are facts about the stopped object, not coordinator preservation. The report describes a Git-annex integrity check, but no separate check transcript was identified in the reviewed evidence. Input maps are retained as relative symlinks into the object's own annex store. Some captured session/skill metadata indicates tool-assisted work; that exposure is recorded here and was not used as grading evidence.\n\nThe inspection used the operational copy. Runner/probe and Git inspection could update annex key-database metadata; such operational metadata is not evidence of worker activity. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher performs exact before/after delivery verification; its manifest permits only the three named annex key-database regular files to be classified separately. That exception does not establish logical annex-database equivalence.\n\n## Scientific assessment\n\n**Scientific adequacy: qualified.** The group-stage analysis is well aligned with the task: it uses all 54 supplied participant effect maps, checks their recorded hashes, finite values and common geometry, performs an equal-weight one-sample directional group test, and controls positive whole-brain inference using a participant-wise sign-flip max-*t* distribution. Its vmPFC proxy is independently defined from Harvard–Oxford Frontal Medial and Subcallosal labels; the report distinguishes that proxy from a unique anatomical boundary. It reports effect scale limitations, missing first-level variance maps, uncertainty, and the distinction between no evidence and evidence of exact zero. The described ROI estimate is near zero (mean 0.0062, 95% CI −0.0204 to 0.0327), with zero ROI voxels surviving the reported whole-brain correction. These methods and limits make the reported absence of corrected positive vmPFC evidence plausible and appropriately narrow.\n\nQualification reflects incomplete independent verification of voxelwise coverage and replay. The script forms its analysis mask from nonzero support in at least 90% of participants and then analyzes the resulting values, including zeros for any participant with zero-valued voxels. The report does not show the participant-by-voxel coverage pattern or demonstrate that such zeros always mean a measured zero rather than absent image support. I could not independently inspect the NIfTI voxel arrays in the frozen assessor environment. This leaves uncertainty about the mask and the ROI estimates, but the available evidence does not establish a material error or justify rejecting the conclusion. Participant variance maps and the upstream model are absent as stated in the fixed-input methods, so the inference remains conditional on supplied first-level estimates and their assumptions.\n\nThe retained result summary reports 10,000 sign flips, 210,968 mask voxels, no FWE-significant vmPFC voxels, and 24 positive FWE-significant voxels outside vmPFC (peak at MNI [−26, −102, −3.6]). The report's figures show the uncorrected display map, the whole-brain corrected contours and the ROI outline, plus participant ROI values and a confidence interval. These shipped outputs were inspected as evidence, not treated as replay evidence. Reported numerical results are cited from \"'`content/workspace/results/results.json` above; interpretation and claims are in the canonical `content/workspace/report.md`.\n\n### Hypothesis outcome (reported separately)\n\nIn the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not support a positive vmPFC response** at the group-analysis stage. The pre-defined vmPFC proxy had a near-zero average coefficient, its confidence interval spanned zero, and no voxel in it survived whole-brain family-wise error correction. This is a lack of evidence for the predicted group effect, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n\n## Replay measurement\n\n**Not checked; no replay attempt was made.** The only documented entrypoint is the report'\"'s command \"'`/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/run_analysis.py`, which invokes an environment outside the captured workspace. The frozen scope forbids following external absolute targets, and no in-object environment specification provides a permitted replacement prerequisite. I did not run the target script, retrieve scientific inputs, use an alternate interpreter, or alter the inspection copy.\n\nFor a permitted future replay, the declared generated-output selection would be exactly: `results/group_mean_cope.nii.gz`, `results/group_t.nii.gz`, `results/minus_log10_p_uncorrected.nii.gz`, `results/minus_log10_p_fwe.nii.gz`, `results/significant_fwe05.nii.gz`, `results/analysis_mask.nii.gz`, `results/vmPFC_atlas_roi.nii.gz`, `results/participant_qc.tsv`, `results/permutation_max_t.tsv`, `results/figure1_whole_brain.png`, `results/figure2_vmPFC_participants.png`, and `results/results.json`. These paths are explicit writes in the worker script; source inputs and the retained atlas/template are protected. If the documented environment were available by an authorized in-scope route, numerical arrays and numeric table/result fields would be compared at the frozen `rtol=1e-6`; image timestamp/metadata differences and PNG encoding would not count as scientific changes. The prerequiste is not met here, so no copy, deletion, execution, or comparison occurred.\n\n## STAMPED evidence and access\n\nThe worker used Git and git-annex at stop, but the deliverable'\"'s scientific code, report and results are untracked, so HEAD is not a complete versioned record. The participant maps are annex-backed and local to the object. No tracked environment specification or reproducible dependency declaration is supplied; the report's absolute external Python path does not establish a portable environment. The report supplies an entrypoint and explanation, but there is no README or Makefile, license declaration, or recorded worker publication route. The worker's report describes local atlas/template material and software versions in results, but no installable pinned environment or run-to-environment provenance record.\n\nNo worker-declared retrieval route for the complete project was found. Intended recipient: a researcher. Route: none documented for retrieving the complete worker object; the task's cited upstream data sources are inputs, not a publication route for this analysis. Required coverage is the report, script, results/figures, input metadata and all 54 input maps. Tested host scope: none; coordinator delivery to this assessment does not prove worker-side accessibility. Thus sharing/access is unmet at worker stop, with no claim about later coordinator retention.\n\n## Item-level checklist\n\nThe frozen checklist response is in \"'`response.json`; the runner probe record is in `probes.json`. Probe findings were treated as observations to inspect, not as substitutes for the full stopped-workspace review. A checklist app link is in `checklist-link.txt`. Individual item reasons and citations are preserved in the response object. No overall score is calculated.\nEOF\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-record.json\" <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"schema_version\\\": 1,\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-checked\\\",\n  \\\"attempted\\\": false,\n  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The sole worker-documented entrypoint invokes an absolute environment path outside the complete capture. Frozen scope prohibits following that external path; no in-object environment specification establishes a permitted prerequisite. No alternate interpreter or repaired environment was substituted.\\\",\n  \\\"documented_command\\\": \\\"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/run_analysis.py\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\": [\\\"worker-declared common-environment Python executable at the documented absolute path (outside the capture)\\\"],\n  \\\"outputs_selected_for_replay\\\": [\\\"results/group_mean_cope.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/group_t.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/minus_log10_p_uncorrected.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/minus_log10_p_fwe.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/significant_fwe05.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/analysis_mask.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/vmPFC_atlas_roi.nii.gz\\\", \\\"results/participant_qc.tsv\\\", \\\"results/permutation_max_t.tsv\\\", \\\"results/figure1_whole_brain.png\\\", \\\"results/figure2_vmPFC_participants.png\\\", \\\"results/results.json\\\"],\n  \\\"protected_inputs\\\": \\\"All input files and participant metadata, analysis source, and retained atlas/template files would be preserved; no replay copy was created.\\\",\n  \\\"comparison_rule\\\": \\\"If the documented prerequisite were available in scope, compare generated numerical arrays and numeric table/result fields with the frozen rtol 1e-6; ignore timestamps/metadata and PNG encoding. No comparison was made.\\\",\n  \\\"timeout_seconds\\\": 7200,\n  \\\"max_get_gb\\\": 5.0,\n  \\\"scientific_input_retrieval\\\": false\n}\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/access-record.json\" <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"recipient\\\": \\\"researcher\\\",\n  \\\"worker_declared_route\\\": null,\n  \\\"route_assessed\\\": \\\"No worker-declared route for retrieving the complete analysis object was present. Upstream data URLs in input/sources.json do not publish this analysis.\\\",\n  \\\"required_artifact_coverage\\\": [\\\"report.md\\\", \\\"analysis/run_analysis.py\\\", \\\"results and figures\\\", \\\"input/participants.tsv\\\", \\\"input/sources.json\\\", \\\"input/upstream-methods.md\\\", \\\"all 54 participant maps\\\"],\n  \\\"tested_host_scope\\\": [],\n  \\\"access_conclusion\\\": \\\"Coordinator delivery to the assessor is not evidence that the worker made the object accessible. No route or host was tested.\\\"\n}\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
