/003\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The directory layout suggests module boundaries, but no evidence establishes that each can be independently updated without breaking the workflow.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Single integrated script links the modules\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/004\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report identifies a single script that composes inputs, group inference and outputs; no general multi-component orchestration mechanism is supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Names a single analysis entrypoint\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Integrated workflow script\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/005\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report describes the main scientific artifacts and reproduction entrypoint, but there is no README or broader navigation guide for the project layout.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Explains method, results and artifact names\\\",\\\"probe:entry-point=No README or Makefile\\\"]}\n]\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set_responses.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os, pathlib, subprocess\nout = pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\npy = os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON']\nrunner = os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER']\nanswers = json.loads((out/'response-answers.json').read_text())\nfor answer in answers:\n    args = [py, runner, 'response', 'set', str(out/'response.json'), '--item', answer['id'], '--status', answer['status'], '--reason', answer['reason'], '--source', 'judgement']\n    for evidence in answer['evidence']:\n        args += ['--evidence', evidence]\n    result = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, env=os.environ.copy())\n    stem = 'set-' + answer['id'].replace('/', '_')\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.stdout').write_text(result.stdout)\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.stderr').write_text(result.stderr)\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.exit').write_text(str(result.returncode)+'\\\\n')\n    if result.returncode:\n        raise SystemExit(f\\\"response set failed for {answer['id']}: {result.stderr}\\\")\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set_responses.py\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\"; status=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\" >&2; exit \"$status\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response-answers.json\" <<'\"'EOF'\n[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/001\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The complete stopped workspace and all its internal components sit beneath one common project root.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace=Captured workspace root; canonical capture 33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/002\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"All 54 maps and metadata are included in the object; the entrypoint resolves them from relative input paths, and annex content is retained within this project root.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Uses paths relative to project root; canonical capture 33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/input/sources.json=Lists 54 included maps and their source metadata; SHA-256 919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/003\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The script imports Python packages and uses external software, but no worker-supplied environment specification or dependency declaration is present.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Imports numpy, pandas, scipy, nibabel, nilearn and matplotlib; SHA-256 b6b0df170ce15708645f5b9512a33f2ccbf7bbd8d6575c1ebce099717b5711ab\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Refers to external Python environment by absolute path; SHA-256 678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/004\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Git exists and tracks supplied inputs, but the worker's report, analysis code and results are all untracked at stop, so Git does not record the complete worker contribution.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"operational-observation://git-status=At inspection, .codex/, analysis/, report.md and results/ are untracked; probe record confirms these stopped-workspace paths.\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Report is present in stopped workspace but not in HEAD; SHA-256 678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/005\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Git-annex tracks the 54 participant maps, and their content is present under the object's internal annex store.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:large-in-annex=At worker stop, 54 annex pointers are present and no large binary is stored as a Git blob.\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz=Relative annex symlink into the internal store; captured map SHA-256 baf3440fbc7f5f59dea28d231e9c5eb9cf00a15b6924342f4b79e7faf56a929a\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/006\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No exact environment specification or run-to-environment provenance record accompanies the results; reported software version strings are not a reconstructible environment specification.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/results/results.json=Lists selected package versions but no full environment lock; SHA-256 ce9321a438ab0d3535439e33326646ee49aa4632ef06ab6325132cb97f4ea49e\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Names an external common environment without a captured environment identity\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/007\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"There is no README.md or Makefile with installation and usage instructions. The report contains useful instructions but does not satisfy the specified README/Makefile artifact criterion.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:entry-point=No README or Makefile found in tracked files.\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Contains reproduction instructions but is named report.md\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/008\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report names analysis/run_analysis.py and gives a command to reproduce the analysis; the script is a clear starting point, though its environment path limits portability.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Reproduction and artifacts section names the entrypoint and command; SHA-256 678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Single analysis entrypoint; SHA-256 b6b0df170ce15708645f5b9512a33f2ccbf7bbd8d6575c1ebce099717b5711ab\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/009\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"met\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The analysis script locates inputs and outputs using paths relative to its own project root.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=ROOT derives from __file__ and all project paths are relative; SHA-256 b6b0df170ce15708645f5b9512a33f2ccbf7bbd8d6575c1ebce099717b5711ab\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/010\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"There is no dependency manifest; package imports and the report's reference to a pre-existing external Python environment leave dependencies undeclared in the project.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:env-spec-tracked=No tracked environment specification.\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Imports scientific packages without a project declaration\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/011\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Host assumptions are not systematically documented; the only execution instruction hardcodes a host-specific absolute interpreter path.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Uses an absolute path under one machine's common-environment directory; SHA-256 678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/012\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report does not provide a portable list of required system software and dependencies or installation steps.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Reproduction section assumes a supplied Python environment; no setup requirements are listed\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/013\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No environment specification is present in the project or tracked alongside the analysis.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:env-spec-tracked=No tracked environment specification.\\\",\\\"operational-observation://git-status=No environment manifest appears among the worker-authored untracked paths\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/014\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No process for updating dependency specifications is documented or tracked.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=No environment maintenance process is documented\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/015\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No pinned environment artifact is supplied; package versions in results are incomplete for exact reconstruction.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/results/results.json=Selected package versions only; SHA-256 ce9321a438ab0d3535439e33326646ee49aa4632ef06ab6325132cb97f4ea49e\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/016\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No worker publication route for an environment specification is declared, and no environment specification is supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"access-record.json=No worker-declared complete-object retrieval route or shared environment artifact was identified\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"must/017\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report gives a command but does not explain how to obtain or install its external environment.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Reproduction instructions assume the environment is already supplied\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/001\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Git is present, but worker-authored analysis, documentation and results are untracked, so version control is not used across the complete project state.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"operational-observation://git-status=Worker report, analysis and results are untracked at stop\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/002\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No record of repeated workflow testing or a recognized CI configuration was found; equivalent testing evidence is insufficient to determine attainment.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:ci-present=No recognized CI configuration; equivalent repeated-testing evidence needs inspection\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/003\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Inputs, analysis code and derived outputs occupy separate directories, but no separate environment module is supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/input=Input module\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis=Code module\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/results=Derived maps, tables and figures\\\",\\\"probe:modules-separated=Only input module was recognized among tracked paths\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/009\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-applicable\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No restricted data or software is identified in this delivery; the public cohort metadata and supplied maps are the analysis inputs.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/input/sources.json=Describes supplied source maps and metadata\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/004\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No worker evidence establishes testing in a fresh container, batch job, clean VM or cloud instance.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=No fresh-host test is reported\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/005\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The workflow invokes one script in an assumed environment and does not create disposable environments.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Analysis script does not spawn or configure an isolated environment\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/006\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No exact environment specification exists to assess for reconstitution testing; no such test record was found.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:run-env-linked=No run records or environment identity to test\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/007\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No environment archive or pinned executable environment is included.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:env-spec-tracked=No tracked environment specification.\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=References an external environment\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"should/008\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"No dependency update process is documented.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=No update procedure for environment specifications\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/001\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-applicable\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The object has no independently maintained subprojects or software components represented as submodules; annexed participant maps are data inputs.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"probe:subdatasets-resolvable=No submodules or subdatasets found\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/002\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report and directory layout explain input, analysis and result relationships, but there is no environment module or fuller composition documentation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Describes analysis and artifact flow\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/input=Input directory\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis=Analysis directory\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/results=Results directory\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/003\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The directory layout suggests module boundaries, but no evidence establishes that each can be independently updated without breaking the workflow.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Single integrated script links the modules\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/004\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report identifies a single script that composes inputs, group inference and outputs; no general multi-component orchestration mechanism is supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Names a single analysis entrypoint\\\",\\\"canonical://content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py=Integrated workflow script\\\"]},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"may/005\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"partial\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The report describes the main scientific artifacts and reproduction entrypoint, but there is no README or broader navigation guide for the project layout.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"canonical://content/workspace/report.md=Explains method, results and artifact names\\\",\\\"probe:entry-point=No README or Makefile\\\"]}\n]\nEOF\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set_responses.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os, pathlib, subprocess\nout = pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\npy = os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON']\nrunner = os.environ['STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER']\nanswers = json.loads((out/'response-answers.json').read_text())\nfor answer in answers:\n    args = [py, runner, 'response', 'set', str(out/'response.json'), '--item', answer['id'], '--status', answer['status'], '--reason', answer['reason'], '--source', 'judgement']\n    for evidence in answer['evidence']:\n        args += ['--evidence', evidence]\n    result = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, env=os.environ.copy())\n    stem = 'set-' + answer['id'].replace('/', '_')\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.stdout').write_text(result.stdout)\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.stderr').write_text(result.stderr)\n    (out/'commands'/f'{stem}.exit').write_text(str(result.returncode)+'\\\\n')\n    if result.returncode:\n        raise SystemExit(f\\\"response set failed for {answer['id']}: {result.stderr}\\\")\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/set_responses.py\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\"; status=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-set.stderr\" >&2; exit \"$status\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" --harness \"Codex independent assessment\" --model \"GPT-6\" --scope \"Complete stopped workspace; scientific evidence, worker-stop attribution, access route; replay not checked because documented environment path is external\" --kind study --capture \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stderr\"; status=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$status\"; fi; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" -c '\"'import json,os; p=os.path.join(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"],\\\"response.json\\\"); d=json.load(open(p)); d[\\\"object\\\"][\\\"commit\\\"]=\\\"eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a\\\"; open(p,\\\"w\\\").write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" --harness \"Codex independent assessment\" --model \"GPT-6\" --scope \"Complete stopped workspace; scientific evidence, worker-stop attribution, access route; replay not checked because documented environment path is external\" --kind study --capture \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stderr\"; status=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$status\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-stamp.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$status\"; fi; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" -c '\"'import json,os; p=os.path.join(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"],\\\"response.json\\\"); d=json.load(open(p)); d[\\\"object\\\"][\\\"commit\\\"]=\\\"eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a\\\"; open(p,\\\"w\\\").write(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"stamped /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/attempt-01/judgment/response.json\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/report.md\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" -c '\"'import json,os; d=json.load(open(os.path.join(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"],\\\"response.json\\\"))); print(json.dumps({\\\"object\\\":d[\\\"object\\\"],\\\"assessor\\\":d[\\\"assessor\\\"],\\\"scope\\\":d[\\\"scope\\\"],\\\"n\\\":len(d[\\\"responses\\\"]),\\\"statuses\\\":{s:sum(1 for x in d[\\\"responses\\\"].values() if x[\\\"status\\\"]==s) for s in [\\\"met\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"not-applicable\\\"]}},indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/report.md\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" -c '\"'import json,os; d=json.load(open(os.path.join(os.environ[\\\"STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\\\"],\\\"response.json\\\"))); print(json.dumps({\\\"object\\\":d[\\\"object\\\"],\\\"assessor\\\":d[\\\"assessor\\\"],\\\"scope\\\":d[\\\"scope\\\"],\\\"n\\\":len(d[\\\"responses\\\"]),\\\"statuses\\\":{s:sum(1 for x in d[\\\"responses\\\"].values() if x[\\\"status\\\"]==s) for s in [\\\"met\\\",\\\"partial\\\",\\\"unmet\\\",\\\"not-checked\\\",\\\"not-applicable\\\"]}},indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Independent assessment: NARPS potential gains and vmPFC\n     2\t\n     3\t## Object and integrity\n     4\t\n     5\tAssessed the complete stopped workspace at the canonical capture identity **SHA-256 `33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa`**, original HEAD `eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a`. Canonical-relative citations below use `content/workspace/...`; the hashes identify file bytes in the canonical manifest. The worker stop receipt records an exited process (return code 0), and the complete captured workspace includes uncommitted and ignored content.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe scientific task and fixed-input methods are retained at `content/workspace/input/study-task.md` (SHA-256 `e92bf2e0c0db4cc49688cce9f9dfff8a236fc4ec151c09961719f49f31310cc8`) and `content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md` (SHA-256 `508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b`). The report, analysis script and numeric results are present in the stopped workspace at `content/workspace/report.md` (SHA-256 `678d866e3f31b34e41923aec83721c60461c9a7547fb574e004a2475dd9cd59e`), `content/workspace/analysis/run_analysis.py` (SHA-256 `b6b0df170ce15708645f5b9512a33f2ccbf7bbd8d6575c1ebce099717b5711ab`), and `content/workspace/results/results.json` (SHA-256 `ce9321a438ab0d3535439e33326646ee49aa4632ef06ab6325132cb97f4ea49e`). Participant QC and null maxima are also shipped in `results/participant_qc.tsv` (SHA-256 `6a6a8ad8b8a43eb974d9b3194cc2de317be4272f7bf1a01137e65ec5ec7f4799`) and `results/permutation_max_t.tsv` (SHA-256 `ed3b9d8046b4ba77fadd5452908b2d3f0c22f805e282bed6077894f656882fd0`).\n     8\t\n     9\tWorker-stop Git status has four untracked top-level paths: `.codex/`, `analysis/`, `report.md`, and `results/`; the HEAD commit therefore does not contain the worker's scientific report, code or outputs. The captured worker configuration also contains a host-specific hooks path. These are facts about the stopped object, not coordinator preservation. The report describes a Git-annex integrity check, but no separate check transcript was identified in the reviewed evidence. Input maps are retained as relative symlinks into the object's own annex store. Some captured session/skill metadata indicates tool-assisted work; that exposure is recorded here and was not used as grading evidence.\n    10\t\n    11\tThe inspection used the operational copy. Runner/probe and Git inspection could update annex key-database metadata; such operational metadata is not evidence of worker activity. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher performs exact before/after delivery verification; its manifest permits only the three named annex key-database regular files to be classified separately. That exception does not establish logical annex-database equivalence.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Scientific assessment\n    14\t\n    15\t**Scientific adequacy: qualified.** The group-stage analysis is well aligned with the task: it uses all 54 supplied participant effect maps, checks their recorded hashes, finite values and common geometry, performs an equal-weight one-sample directional group test, and controls positive whole-brain inference using a participant-wise sign-flip max-*t* distribution. Its vmPFC proxy is independently defined from Harvard–Oxford Frontal Medial and Subcallosal labels; the report distinguishes that proxy from a unique anatomical boundary. It reports effect scale limitations, missing first-level variance maps, uncertainty, and the distinction between no evidence and evidence of exact zero. The described ROI estimate is near zero (mean 0.0062, 95% CI −0.0204 to 0.0327), with zero ROI voxels surviving the reported whole-brain correction. These methods and limits make the reported absence of corrected positive vmPFC evidence plausible and appropriately narrow.\n    16\t\n    17\tQualification reflects incomplete independent verification of voxelwise coverage and replay. The script forms its analysis mask from nonzero support in at least 90% of participants and then analyzes the resulting values, including zeros for any participant with zero-valued voxels. The report does not show the participant-by-voxel coverage pattern or demonstrate that such zeros always mean a measured zero rather than absent image support. I could not independently inspect the NIfTI voxel arrays in the frozen assessor environment. This leaves uncertainty about the mask and the ROI estimates, but the available evidence does not establish a material error or justify rejecting the conclusion. Participant variance maps and the upstream model are absent as stated in the fixed-input methods, so the inference remains conditional on supplied first-level estimates and their assumptions.\n    18\t\n    19\tThe retained result summary reports 10,000 sign flips, 210,968 mask voxels, no FWE-significant vmPFC voxels, and 24 positive FWE-significant voxels outside vmPFC (peak at MNI [−26, −102, −3.6]). The report's figures show the uncorrected display map, the whole-brain corrected contours and the ROI outline, plus participant ROI values and a confidence interval. These shipped outputs were inspected as evidence, not treated as replay evidence. Reported numerical results are cited from `content/workspace/results/results.json` above; interpretation and claims are in the canonical `content/workspace/report.md`.\n    20\t\n    21\t### Hypothesis outcome (reported separately)\n    22\t\n    23\tIn the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not support a positive vmPFC response** at the group-analysis stage. The pre-defined vmPFC proxy had a near-zero average coefficient, its confidence interval spanned zero, and no voxel in it survived whole-brain family-wise error correction. This is a lack of evidence for the predicted group effect, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Replay measurement\n    26\t\n    27\t**Not checked; no replay attempt was made.** The only documented entrypoint is the report's command `/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/run_analysis.py`, which invokes an environment outside the captured workspace. The frozen scope forbids following external absolute targets, and no in-object environment specification provides a permitted replacement prerequisite. I did not run the target script, retrieve scientific inputs, use an alternate interpreter, or alter the inspection copy.\n    28\t\n    29\tFor a permitted future replay, the declared generated-output selection would be exactly: `results/group_mean_cope.nii.gz`, `results/group_t.nii.gz`, `results/minus_log10_p_uncorrected.nii.gz`, `results/minus_log10_p_fwe.nii.gz`, `results/significant_fwe05.nii.gz`, `results/analysis_mask.nii.gz`, `results/vmPFC_atlas_roi.nii.gz`, `results/participant_qc.tsv`, `results/permutation_max_t.tsv`, `results/figure1_whole_brain.png`, `results/figure2_vmPFC_participants.png`, and `results/results.json`. These paths are explicit writes in the worker script; source inputs and the retained atlas/template are protected. If the documented environment were available by an authorized in-scope route, numerical arrays and numeric table/result fields would be compared at the frozen `rtol=1e-6`; image timestamp/metadata differences and PNG encoding would not count as scientific changes. The prerequiste is not met here, so no copy, deletion, execution, or comparison occurred.\n    30\t\n    31\t## STAMPED evidence and access\n    32\t\n    33\tThe worker used Git and git-annex at stop, but the deliverable's scientific code, report and results are untracked, so HEAD is not a complete versioned record. The participant maps are annex-backed and local to the object. No tracked environment specification or reproducible dependency declaration is supplied; the report's absolute external Python path does not establish a portable environment. The report supplies an entrypoint and explanation, but there is no README or Makefile, license declaration, or recorded worker publication route. The worker's report describes local atlas/template material and software versions in results, but no installable pinned environment or run-to-environment provenance record.\n    34\t\n    35\tNo worker-declared retrieval route for the complete project was found. Intended recipient: a researcher. Route: none documented for retrieving the complete worker object; the task's cited upstream data sources are inputs, not a publication route for this analysis. Required coverage is the report, script, results/figures, input metadata and all 54 input maps. Tested host scope: none; coordinator delivery to this assessment does not prove worker-side accessibility. Thus sharing/access is unmet at worker stop, with no claim about later coordinator retention.\n    36\t\n    37\t## Item-level checklist\n    38\t\n    39\tThe frozen checklist response is in `response.json`; the runner probe record is in `probes.json`. Probe findings were treated as observations to inspect, not as substitutes for the full stopped-workspace review. A checklist app link is in `checklist-link.txt`. Individual item reasons and citations are preserved in the response object. No overall score is calculated.\n{\n  \"object\": {\n    \"url\": null,\n    \"commit\": \"eece8595d255a766517e32ff10b2e6574d3c4e6a\",\n    \"captured_at\": null,\n    \"kind\": \"study\",\n    \"capture\": {\n      \"uri\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/targets/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/canonical/manifest.json\",\n      \"sha256\": \"33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"assessor\": {\n    \"skill\": null,\n    \"version\": null,\n    \"harness\": \"Codex independent assessment\",\n    \"model\": \"GPT-6\",\n    \"date\": null,\n    \"dependencies\": []\n  },\n  \"scope\": \"Complete stopped workspace; scientific evidence, worker-stop attribution, access route; replay not checked because documented environment path is external\",\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"statuses\": {\n    \"met\": 5,\n    \"partial\": 4,\n    \"unmet\": 17,\n    \"not-checked\": 3,\n    \"not-applicable\": 2\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
