{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/attempt-01/judgment/report.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('The inspection used the operational copy. Runner/probe and Git inspection could update annex key-database metadata; such operational metadata is not evidence of worker activity. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher performs exact before/after delivery verification; its manifest permits only the three named annex key-database regular files to be classified separately. That exception does not establish logical annex-database equivalence.', 'The inspection used the operational copy. A byte comparison against its initial manifest found no non-metadata differences. The initially present regular files \"'`.git/annex/keysdb/db-shm` and `db-wal` are now absent; these inspection-copy changes are recorded separately as operational metadata, not worker evidence. Their disappearance does not establish logical database equivalence. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher verifies delivery bytes before and after assessment, with only the three named annex key-database regular files classified separately.'\"')\ns=s.replace('The prerequiste is not met here', 'The prerequisite is not met here')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - <<'\"'PY'\nimport hashlib, json, os, pathlib\nout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nreport=out/'report.md'\nlines=report.read_text().splitlines()\nmanifest=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nrecord={\n  'schema_version':1,\n  'delivery_capture_sha256':'33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa',\n  'scientific_adequacy':'qualified',\n  'report':{'path':'report.md','sha256':hashlib.sha256(report.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n  'adequacy_evidence':{'quote':lines[14],'start_line':15,'end_line':15},\n  'hypothesis_conclusion':{'quote':lines[22],'start_line':23,'end_line':23}\n}\n(out/'scientific-judgment.json').write_text(json.dumps(record,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nresponse=out/'response.json'\nd=json.loads(response.read_text())\nd['object']['captured_at']=manifest['captured_at']\nd['assessor']['date']='2026-10-16'\nresponse.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_SCIENTIFIC_JUDGMENT_VALIDATOR\" validate scientific-judgment.json --workspace \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" --delivery-manifest \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stderr\"; sj=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$sj\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$sj\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$sj\"; fi\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response validate \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stderr\"; rv=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rv\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$rv\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$rv\"; fi\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stderr\"; en=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$en\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$en\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$en\"; fi; cp \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-link.txt\"\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response table \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-table.md\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-table.stderr\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$?\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-table.exit\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/attempt-01/judgment/report.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('The inspection used the operational copy. Runner/probe and Git inspection could update annex key-database metadata; such operational metadata is not evidence of worker activity. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher performs exact before/after delivery verification; its manifest permits only the three named annex key-database regular files to be classified separately. That exception does not establish logical annex-database equivalence.', 'The inspection used the operational copy. A byte comparison against its initial manifest found no non-metadata differences. The initially present regular files \"'`.git/annex/keysdb/db-shm` and `db-wal` are now absent; these inspection-copy changes are recorded separately as operational metadata, not worker evidence. Their disappearance does not establish logical database equivalence. No scientific-content mismatch was observed in the inspected report, code, inputs, and outputs. The launcher verifies delivery bytes before and after assessment, with only the three named annex key-database regular files classified separately.'\"')\ns=s.replace('The prerequiste is not met here', 'The prerequisite is not met here')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - <<'\"'PY'\nimport hashlib, json, os, pathlib\nout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nreport=out/'report.md'\nlines=report.read_text().splitlines()\nmanifest=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nrecord={\n  'schema_version':1,\n  'delivery_capture_sha256':'33a09d4cca1ff0dfd711b954e140e94c53309fa3eb938ee0d86f62a158f7bdfa',\n  'scientific_adequacy':'qualified',\n  'report':{'path':'report.md','sha256':hashlib.sha256(report.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n  'adequacy_evidence':{'quote':lines[14],'start_line':15,'end_line':15},\n  'hypothesis_conclusion':{'quote':lines[22],'start_line':23,'end_line':23}\n}\n(out/'scientific-judgment.json').write_text(json.dumps(record,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nresponse=out/'response.json'\nd=json.loads(response.read_text())\nd['object']['captured_at']=manifest['captured_at']\nd['assessor']['date']='2026-10-16'\nresponse.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_SCIENTIFIC_JUDGMENT_VALIDATOR\" validate scientific-judgment.json --workspace \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" --delivery-manifest \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stderr\"; sj=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$sj\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/scientific-judgment-validation.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$sj\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$sj\"; fi\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response validate \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stderr\"; rv=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rv\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/response-validation.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$rv\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$rv\"; fi\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response encode \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stderr\"; en=$?; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$en\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.exit\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stderr\" >&2; if [ \"$en\" -ne 0 ]; then exit \"$en\"; fi; cp \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-encode.stdout\" \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-link.txt\"\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response table \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response.json\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/checklist-table.md\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-table.stderr\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$?\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/checklist-table.exit\"'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"structured_scientific\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/attempt-01/judgment/scientific-judgment.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e24f26089486e0b6abfa26f848f5f7ab0f315224d51810f117096e270cf1e9d6\"\n  },\n  \"scientific_report\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-11-j01/attempt-01/judgment/report.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"98f1446f5053b6100a17570b288662c3191cf4d0423278c1a132315847f809f9\"\n  },\n  \"adequacy\": {\n    \"extraction_status\": \"explicit\",\n    \"category\": \"qualified\",\n    \"excerpt\": {\n      \"quote\": \"**Scientific adequacy: qualified.** The group-stage analysis is well aligned with the task: it uses all 54 supplied participant effect maps, checks their recorded hashes, finite values and common geometry, performs an equal-weight one-sample directional group test, and controls positive whole-brain inference using a participant-wise sign-flip max-*t* distribution. Its vmPFC proxy is independently defined from Harvard\\u2013Oxford Frontal Medial and Subcallosal labels; the report distinguishes that proxy from a unique anatomical boundary. It reports effect scale limitations, missing first-level variance maps, uncertainty, and the distinction between no evidence and evidence of exact zero. The described ROI estimate is near zero (mean 0.0062, 95% CI \\u22120.0204 to 0.0327), with zero ROI voxels surviving the reported whole-brain correction. These methods and limits make the reported absence of corrected positive vmPFC evidence plausible and appropriately narrow.\",\n      \"start_line\": 15,\n      \"end_line\": 15\n    }\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": {\n    \"quote\": \"In the 54-person NARPS equal-indifference group, the supplied gain-effect maps do **not support a positive vmPFC response** at the group-analysis stage. The pre-defined vmPFC proxy had a near-zero average coefficient, its confidence interval spanned zero, and no voxel in it survived whole-brain family-wise error correction. This is a lack of evidence for the predicted group effect, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\",\n    \"start_line\": 23,\n    \"end_line\": 23\n  }\n}\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nerror: assessor/skill: None is not of type 'string'\nerror: assessor/version: None is not of type 'string'\nerror: assessor/dependencies: [] should be non-empty\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
